Criteria (from the brief): (a) never crashes; (b) all 8 starts of fit 1 and of fit 2 agree, target S <= 0.1.
Operational definitions used for step 2:
 - (a) met  <=> no start of fit 1 or fit 2 has a failed round (Py-BOBYQA/scipy unsuccessful, cobaya 'Minimization failed!', or any exception).
 - (b) met  <=> all 8 starts of each fit produce a result (end on the 0.001 stop rule or the 5-round cap) and
               S = max - min total chi2 over the 8 final results <= 0.1, separately for fit 1 and for fit 2.
Best candidate:
 1. among candidates meeting (a) and (b): fewest total evaluations (fit 1 + fit 2);
 2. if none meets both: run candidate (iv) (brief); for steps 3-4 use the candidate meeting (a) with the smallest
    max(S fit1, S fit2); if none meets (a), the one with the fewest failed starts, then the smallest max S.
 3. If a candidate is still running when the others have finished and one of the finished ones meets (a) and (b),
    the choice is made among the finished candidates and this is recorded; the running one is still reported in full.

